-- the vestibule of Counter's assay: the disagreements between the walker's word and the treaty as it stands, each
-- a statement in the assay's own terms and the darkness it waits on. read by bin/counter book.

-- potential time (isaac, 2026-09-23, on the cone: "proper time is the fuel, and ✦ Now is the worldline that has no
-- spacelike component — is this where Counter-as-app comes in?"): the room already has no clock in it. every clock is
-- a winding number, a round is a click per name, and `due` is a residue; so each cycle's winding is its own proper
-- time, potential and not actual, and rest by coverage (`mayRest`) is the same page for one walker. what the room
-- lacks is ✦ Now as a worldline: a clock the round does not click, that winds itself, that nothing in the room reads,
-- so that due can be read against it instead of against a cap. with it the round and EIH's day are one Runner, and
-- the winding number is the fuel `runs` counts. a carrier and two rows.
